@startuml PrintScript_Componentes

title Diagrama de Componentes: PrintScript

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam linetype ortho

legend right
  |= Flecha |= Significado |
  | <b>——▶</b> | depende (api): lo re-expone a quien lo use |
  | <b>- -▶</b> | depende (implementation): uso interno |
  | <b>··▶</b> | solo en tests |
endlegend

package "Entrada" {
  [cli] as CLI
}

package "Orquestacion" {
  [runner] as RUNNER
}

package "Pipeline" {
  [lexer] as LEXER
  [parser] as PARSER
  [semantic] as SEMANTIC
  [interpreter] as INTERPRETER
}

package "Herramientas" {
  [formatter] as FORMATTER
  [linter] as LINTER
}

package "Base" {
  [ast] as AST
  [common] as COMMON
}

note right of COMMON
  Token, TokenType, Position,
  LanguageVersion, ScriptError
  y ConfigParser (json/yaml plano,
  compartido por formatter y linter).
  No depende de nadie.
end note

note right of AST
  Los nodos del arbol y el
  Registry<N, C, R> generico
  que usa el interpreter.
end note

' ===== la base =====
AST --> COMMON

' ===== el pipeline: ninguno conoce al otro, todos hablan por common y ast =====
LEXER --> COMMON
PARSER --> COMMON
PARSER --> AST
SEMANTIC --> AST
SEMANTIC --> COMMON
INTERPRETER --> AST
INTERPRETER ..> COMMON

' ===== las herramientas: tampoco conocen al pipeline =====
FORMATTER --> COMMON
LINTER --> AST
LINTER --> COMMON

' ===== runner: el unico que conoce a todos =====
RUNNER --> LEXER
RUNNER --> PARSER
RUNNER --> SEMANTIC
RUNNER --> INTERPRETER
RUNNER --> FORMATTER
RUNNER --> LINTER
RUNNER --> AST
RUNNER --> COMMON

' ===== cli: entra por runner, no habla con el pipeline =====
CLI ..> RUNNER
CLI ..> COMMON
CLI ..> INTERPRETER
CLI ..> FORMATTER
CLI ..> LINTER

' ===== dependencias que existen solo para los tests =====
FORMATTER ...> LEXER : test
LINTER ...> LEXER : test
LINTER ...> PARSER : test

note as N1
  <b>cli no depende de lexer, parser ni semantic.</b>
  Llega a ellos a traves de runner, que los
  re-expone con api. De interpreter, formatter
  y linter solo usa los tipos que necesita para
  armar las opciones (Output, reglas de config).
end note

CLI .. N1

@enduml
